{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875829-why-is-there-so-much-ooc-drama-in-online-wod-games","id":875829,"title":"Why is there so much OOC drama in online WoD games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-27T12:08:57-07:00","id":875829,"title":"Why is there so much OOC drama in online WoD games?","content":"Every time I go into an online WoD game, there's active OOC drama going on that I have nothing to do with. Nothing short of turning off the OOC channels and staying away from the foyers or the OOC rooms or whatever they're called will assuage this, and even then only to a limited extent.<br /> <br /> What gives? Why do we do this to ourselves? Why is this such a toxic community at times? I do plenty of other things and there's something very distinctively messed up about a lot of people that play these games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10158-thestranjer","name":"TheStranjer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T13:59:37-07:00","id":875957,"title":"","content":"I don't know about online games, have you tried playing with friends and not online ? I've been storytelling Vampire (and Mage but mostly Vampire) with my friends since 1992 and there's nothing toxic about it. It's true that White Wolf was very innovative in turning themes (the inner Beast -Vampire-, epistemology -Mage Ascension- etc.) into roleplaying games. Some of these themes can be very intimate and you'll need a mature troupe in order to cope with them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T14:11:27-07:00","id":875971,"title":"","content":"Its the internet. It has nothing to do with WoD or CofD games. Drama is the natural state of things for humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T14:31:02-07:00","id":875991,"title":"","content":"I can't say I've ever seen a community of roleplayers that didn't have baggage and drama accompanying it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T17:30:10-07:00","id":876134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875829-why-is-there-so-much-ooc-drama-in-online-wod-games?p=875971#post875971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its the internet. It has nothing to do with WoD or CofD games. Drama is the natural state of things for humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div> Exactly. There's even <b><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/GIFT\" target=\"_blank\">an acronym for it.</a></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T18:21:07-07:00","id":876150,"title":"","content":"Where do people even play nwod online? Despite my looking I have been unable to find anything","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T18:29:47-07:00","id":876159,"title":"","content":"People generally play online whey they cannot play offline. There are many reasons for this, but for some, it's because of having a personality that leads into conflicts and is naturally driven towards clashing with other people. For some it's because of inherent competetiveness, for others it's because they find RPG to be their expert niche and &quot;being right&quot; at it is a important component for their self satisfaction and pride. Add the usually faceless and stressful (there is actually a lot of pressure, real or just perceived, to perform in online play at your peak) atmosphere typical to the internet places, and remove the usual factor of simply being friends and having tolerance for each other's negative perks and quirks...and you have a powder keg waiting to go boom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T20:24:33-07:00","id":876218,"title":"","content":"For larger online games, there's also generally a problem of trying to get lots of people with different play-styles together and on the same page to add to this. Even with generally well intentioned people, having a game with 20+ players? It's always a nightmare because you just don't have the ability to have everyone compromise on one vision of how to play the game this time around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T21:45:12-07:00","id":876264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875829-why-is-there-so-much-ooc-drama-in-online-wod-games?p=876218#post876218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For larger online games, there's also generally a problem of trying to get lots of people with different play-styles together and on the same page to add to this. Even with generally well intentioned people, having a game with 20+ players? It's always a nightmare because you just don't have the ability to have everyone compromise on one vision of how to play the game this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forget 20. Four or five can be a huge amount of work. I've ran Pathfinder games for 2 year+ and it is really hard to get a plot to stick together rather than just jumping from combat to combat. CofD is even harder, plus people lose interest and sometime the ones who don't are the ones you wish did. You have to be super picky with who you let into online games if you want them to last.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T01:23:15-07:00","id":876351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStranjer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875829-why-is-there-so-much-ooc-drama-in-online-wod-games#post875829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every time I go into an online WoD game, there's active OOC drama going on that I have nothing to do with. Nothing short of turning off the OOC channels and staying away from the foyers or the OOC rooms or whatever they're called will assuage this, and even then only to a limited extent.<br /> <br /> What gives? Why do we do this to ourselves? Why is this such a toxic community at times? I do plenty of other things and there's something very distinctively messed up about a lot of people that play these games.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the exception of Forest Gump-ing my way into a minor OCC storyteller fight I was not aware of when I played in the first java chats. I've never found internet WoD or OPP settings in general games to be any more or less toxic than other games I've played. The worst I've dealt with is when I used to VtM LARP in the 90's and early 2000's but that drama comes with LARPING in general. And I am curious alongside Mr. FIX. Would love to find a place to play NWoD Online.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T02:06:56-07:00","id":876375,"title":"","content":"I've never noticed this myself. It might just be bad luck in your choice of groups/games? Or good luck on mine?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T02:22:03-07:00","id":876392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875829-why-is-there-so-much-ooc-drama-in-online-wod-games?p=876264#post876264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forget 20. Four or five can be a huge amount of work. I've ran Pathfinder games for 2 year+ and it is really hard to get a plot to stick together rather than just jumping from combat to combat. CofD is even harder, plus people lose interest and sometime the ones who don't are the ones you wish did. You have to be super picky with who you let into online games if you want them to last.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may help you out: <a href=\"http://site.pelgranepress.com/index.php/see-p-xx-four-heroes-and-a-murder-hobo/\" target=\"_blank\">Four Heroes and a Murder Hobo.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T16:13:48-07:00","id":878212,"title":"","content":"This isn't a nwod thing. All persistent world format games suffer from that issue for various reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T19:00:03-07:00","id":878330,"title":"","content":"I'm not so sure about that. I know of games that went on for very long times that weren't plagued by the stuff I've seen. Though it isn't CoD specific. I guess it does happen to some extent, but it's not a constant.<br /> <br /> IME games less prone to these sorts of things have relatively self-correcting settings that don't require significant moderator intervention to return to &quot;normal&quot; after a player does something big, and games that have very strong pull towards specific game play styles. Oddly, an example off the top of my head was a D&amp;D 3 online game... I think it was Forgotten Realms. &quot;We slayed the dragon threatening the main city of the game!&quot; didn't really mean much because it's D&amp;D and there's always another dungeon to crawl. It's not like a CoD game where the PCs have helped overthrow the current Prince for a new NPC one which radically shakes up the setting of the game. D&amp;D also offers a tighter idea of default game play - so PCs largely hung around the town socializing and forming raiding parties - which meant less OOC conflict.<br /> <br /> So I think CoD is structured to fall into the set of games where these issues are the worst. As a toolkit game where players are meant to interact significantly with the setting, there's far less common ground that you're inherently agreeing to just picking a CoD game compared to picking a D&amp;D with one of the official settings.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T19:19:27-07:00","id":878345,"title":"","content":"My first encounter with it online was on a MUD called Nightmare back in the early 90s. It's not really a World of Darkness thing though I agree with Heavy Arms that the social nature of it sort of amplifies it. But I've seen it in online games and online non-games and real life. I'd be surprised if other people hadn't. Or hadn't been a part of it themselves. We are not robots, after all.<br /> <br /> Like the word angst, the term drama has sort of taken on some negative connotations over the years, but there's nothing wrong with getting excited or emotional over things. It's certain persecutory aspects of it that really make things 'toxic,' or as others have noted an over-competitiveness that makes others feel uncomfortable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T08:51:12-07:00","id":884660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStranjer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875829-why-is-there-so-much-ooc-drama-in-online-wod-games#post875829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every time I go into an online WoD game, there's active OOC drama going on that I have nothing to do with. Nothing short of turning off the OOC channels and staying away from the foyers or the OOC rooms or whatever they're called will assuage this, and even then only to a limited extent.<br /> <br /> What gives? Why do we do this to ourselves? Why is this such a toxic community at times? I do plenty of other things and there's something very distinctively messed up about a lot of people that play these games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The simple fact is that the anonymity offered by the online environment simply lets people get their jerk-face on and let rip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T18:31:41-07:00","id":885856,"title":"","content":"I must be lucky, I've only had one online rpg'ing experience with OOC drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}